Harbor: mshtml: the status of a request without a response reads as 0 from IE10 mode on (#100).

XMLHttpRequest.status failed (E_FAIL, a script exception) whenever there was no response: before the request
was sent, and after one that was refused or failed. That is how Internet Explorer behaved up to version 9.
From IE10 on a script gets 0, and pages written for it test for 0 rather than catch: a handler on Office's
add-in Store page read the status of a failed background request and died with an uncaught error.

In IE10 mode and later the property now returns 0 in those cases. Older modes are unchanged.

Test: WindowsTests/mshtml.

--- a/dlls/mshtml/xmlhttprequest.c
+++ b/dlls/mshtml/xmlhttprequest.c
@@ -659,9 +659,11 @@
     if(!p)
         return E_POINTER;
 
+    /* HARBOR HACK: a request without a response (not sent yet, refused, failed) has status 0. Reading that
+     * is an error up to IE9; from IE10 on a script gets the 0, and pages test for it instead of catching. */
     if(This->xhr.ready_state < READYSTATE_LOADED) {
         *p = 0;
-        return E_FAIL;
+        return dispex_compat_mode(&This->xhr.event_target.dispex) >= COMPAT_MODE_IE10 ? S_OK : E_FAIL;
     }
 
     nsres = nsIXMLHttpRequest_GetStatus(This->xhr.nsxhr, &val);
@@ -670,7 +672,7 @@
         return E_FAIL;
     }
     *p = val;
-    if(val == 0)
+    if(val == 0 && dispex_compat_mode(&This->xhr.event_target.dispex) < COMPAT_MODE_IE10)
         return E_FAIL; /* WinAPI thinks this is an error */
 
     return S_OK;
